Security backport (FG-021, approved by orch for the owner 2026-10-25): upstream LibreOffice's
PDF encryption fixes from master (August-September 2026), onto our pin 30742500 (25.8.7.3).
None is on libreoffice-25-8; only aac2961770 is on libreoffice-26-2 (as ff0c1b4fe9).
Unconditional: correctness and confidentiality fixes for every module's PDF export.

Why: FG-021 build #1 measured our protected PDFs (PDF 2.0, AES-256, R6): every encrypted
stream carried /Length = the plaintext length while holding IV + padded ciphertext
(e.g. 375 vs 400 bytes); poppler reported "incorrect stream length" on every file and
refused one ("Incorrect password"), qpdf recovered silently.

Applied in upstream history order (full hashes; master paths vcl/source/pdf/pdfwriter_impl*.cxx
and pdfobjectcopier.cxx are vcl/source/gdi/ on 25.8):
  aac2961770fd  Michael Stahl  2026-08-18  oox,svl,vcl: use more appropriate random numbers
  01de4c02133b  Michael Stahl  2026-08-18  vcl: PDFEncryptorR6: fix subtle off-by-one in computeHashR6
  a3623692c3ab  Michael Stahl  2026-08-19  vcl: fix PDFEncryptorR6 padding
  679f88a775    Michael Stahl  2026-08-19  vcl: PDFEncryptorR6: check result in decryptPerms
  d46d47657e67  Michael Stahl  2026-08-19  vcl: PDF export: fix a bunch of bad /Length with encryption
  0f3a469b25    Michael Stahl  2026-08-19  vcl: PDF export: consistency in stream bracketing
  91970e690b    Michael Stahl  2026-08-19  vcl: PDF export: fix encrypted /Length in PDFObjectCopier
  e0348ccc9e37  Mike Kaganski  2026-09-30  vcl: encrypt the strings a PDF form field and annotation carry
The first four applied cleanly. The other four needed the path mapping above and context
fuzz; two hunks were applied by hand, because 25.8 differs around them:
  d46d47657e hunk 1 (emitTilings): 25.8 casts the length to sal_Int32; now
             calculateStreamSize(...) cast to sal_Int64.
  0f3a469b25 hunk 2 (emitScreenAnnotations): 25.8 builds the EmbeddedFile line with
             separate appends; same change (calculateStreamSize, and the stream bracketed by
             checkAndEnableStreamEncryption / disableStreamEncryption).
Every fuzzed hunk was checked to land in the function upstream changed. e0348ccc9e's commit
message also describes a state-change annotation (/State, /StateModel); the commit has no hunk
for it, and 25.8 writes no such annotation, so nothing was left out.
The vcl/qa unit tests and their data file are omitted (not built here).

